WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.153
Music in one app. Videos in another. Podcasts. Audiobooks. That's four apps.

00:00:06.503 --> 00:00:08.888
Or just one. Omia Player.

00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:15.583
Omia plays the music, videos and audiobooks on your phone, and downloads podcasts to play offline.

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:20.430
And each one gets its own player, built for that kind of listening and watching.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.772
Missing artwork or messy details? Omia looks them up for you.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:31.672
It builds playlists from what you love, and what you haven't played in a while. Or let a few rules build them for you.

00:00:32.022 --> 00:00:35.598
Look up any audiobook's cover, author and description.

00:00:35.948 --> 00:00:40.729
Podcasts get everything you're used to. Subscriptions, a queue, and downloads.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.074
Search everything at once, or just ask.

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:48.411
Voice works in Android Auto too, so your hands stay on the wheel.

00:00:48.761 --> 00:00:51.705
Your listening stats are ready whenever you want them.

00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:57.549
Sharing a phone? Everyone gets their own profile, and can show or hide anything they like.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:02.813
So if you love playing your own media, why juggle four different apps?

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:08.055
Omia Player. One app that does it all. Try it now on Google Play.
